Remove what ZTARC does not have.

Three things upstream offers that we cannot honour, and which a string
substitution cannot fix because they are structure, not wording:

  * "Pangolin Cloud" — there is no ZTARC hosted service. The button is hidden
    in updateUI rather than deleted, so the state machine around it is
    untouched and an upstream rewrite of that machine still applies cleanly.
  * An empty server field — the console is the only way in, so it is prefilled
    from config.DefaultHostname.
  * Terms of Service and Privacy Policy links, in the login window and the
    About tab — ztarc.io has no such pages, and a link that 404s is worse than
    no link. Their declarations go with them, or Go rejects the unused
    variables.
  * "Install CLI" — the binary behind it is the upstream vendor's, fetched from
    their GitHub releases. Renaming the menu entry would have been the dishonest
    fix; it stays hidden until ZTARC has a CLI of its own.

Applied by scripts/rebrand.sh before the sed rules, so the context lines here
match pristine upstream. If fosrl rewrites either file this fails loudly, which
is the intent: the alternative is "Pangolin Cloud" quietly reappearing.

